.TH NEKOSHOT 1 "2026-10-29" "nekoshot 0.10.3" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
nekoshot \- Spectacle-based screenshot and screen recording utility for niri
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B nekoshot
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B nekoshot
is a port of KDE Spectacle to the niri Wayland compositor.  Screenshots are
captured with \fBgrim\fR and niri's IPC; screen, window and region recordings
use niri's Mutter ScreenCast implementation with GStreamer, falling back to
\fBwf-recorder\fR when necessary.
.PP
With no options the configured launch action is used.  A running instance
started with \fB--daemon\fR accepts D-Bus requests from niri key bindings.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-r, \-\-region
Take a rectangular region screenshot (or start a region recording with \fB\-R\fR).
.TP
.B \-m, \-\-current
Capture the focused output.
.TP
.B \-f, \-\-fullscreen
Capture all outputs.
.TP
.B \-a, \-\-active\-window
Capture the focused window.
.TP
.B \-u, \-\-window\-under\-cursor
Pick a window by clicking it and capture that window.
.TP
.B \-l, \-\-launch\-only
Open the interface without taking a screenshot.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-background
Run without opening the viewer unless requested; export and quit.
.TP
.B \-n, \-\-nonotify
Do not show a notification after saving.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-pointer
Include the mouse pointer when the backend supports it.  niri's screencopy
does not composite the cursor into screenshots; recordings use
\fBcursor-mode\fR instead.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-delay \fISECONDS\fR
Wait before capturing.
.TP
.B \-o, \-\-output \fIPATH\fR
Write the screenshot or recording to \fIPATH\fR.
.TP
.B \-R, \-\-record \fIMODE\fR
Start recording.  \fIMODE\fR is \fBr\fR (region), \fBs\fR (screen) or
\fBw\fR (window; opens niri's window picker).
.TP
.B \-\-stop\-recording
Stop the current recording and wait for the file to be finalized.
.TP
.B \-\-daemon
Stay resident and accept D-Bus capture requests.  Combine with niri's
\fBspawn-at-startup\fR for instant key bindings.
.TP
.B \-\-scaled
Capture all outputs at logical resolution instead of native resolution.
.TP
.B \-\-new\-instance
Start a separate process instead of forwarding to the running instance.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-version
Print the version.
.TP
.B \-h, \-\-help
Print help.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/nekoshotrc
Configuration file (KConfig format).
.TP
.I ~/Pictures/Screenshots
Default screenshot location.
.TP
.I ~/Videos/Screencasts
Default recording location.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B NIRI_SOCKET
Used to detect and query the niri compositor.
.TP
.B NEKOSHOT_IMAGE_PLATFORM
Force a screenshot backend; mainly for testing.
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
.B nekoshot \-b \-r \-o /tmp/shot.png \-n
Capture a region headlessly and write it to a file.
.TP
.B nekoshot \-R s
Record the focused output until \fBnekoshot \-\-stop\-recording\fR is called.
.TP
.B nekoshot \-R w
Pick a window with the pointer and record it.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR grim (1),
.BR wf-recorder (1),
.BR niri (1),
.BR gst-launch-1.0 (1)
